.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt GLXGEARS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm glxgears
.Nd ``gears'' demo for GLX
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss "SYNOPSIS"
.Bd -literal
     glxgears [options]
.Ed
.Ss "DESCRIPTION"
.Bd -literal
     The glxgears program is a port of the ``gears'' demo to GLX. It displays
     a set of rotating gears and prints out the frame rate at regular
     intervals. It has become quite popular as basic benchmarking tool.
.Ed
.Ss "OPTIONS"
.Bd -literal
     -display display
             Specify which X display to run on.

     -info   Display OpenGL renderer information.

     -stereo Use a stereo enabled GLX visual.

     -fullscreen
             Run in fullscreen mode.
.Ed
.Ss "AUTHOR"
.Bd -literal
     glxgears was written by Brian Paul <brian.paul@tungstengraphics.com>.

     This manual page was written by Thierry Reding <thierry@gilfi.de>, for
     the Debian project (but may be used by others).
.Ed
